  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Before the staff meeting in the lobby, Katya apologizes to Denis and says she could not sleep all night, while Denis hides the reason he barely slept—until owner Eleonora Andreevna walks in. Listen to the scene.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Привет, Денис.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Ты был расстроен из-за вчерашнего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да нет, всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Прости меня, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Я всю ночь очень переживала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Я совсем сегодня не спала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тоже всю ночь не спал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ворочался всю эту ночь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Понятно, чего ты не выспался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "О любых проблемах сразу сообщать мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "А вот и владелица нашего отеля.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "Я сюда не знакомиться пришла.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Привет, Денис.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hi, Denis.' Katya brings out the contrast between 'hello' and 'Denis' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hi, Katya.' Denis anchors the line on 'hello', while 'Katya' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Ты был расстроен из-за вчерашнего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You were upset because of yesterday.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'yesterday's' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Denis answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да нет, всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, everything is fine.' The meaning hinges on 'yes' working together with 'normally' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Прости меня, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Forgive me, please.' In Russian, the idea of 'forgive' flows naturally into 'please' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Я всю ночь очень переживала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I was very worried all night.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'I was worried' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Я совсем сегодня не спала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not sleep at all today.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'slept' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тоже всю ночь не спал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not sleep all night either.' Denis anchors the line on 'I', while 'slept' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ворочался всю эту ночь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I tossed and turned all night long.' The grammar packs 'tossed and turned' and 'night' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Katya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Понятно, чего ты не выспался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is clear why you did not get enough sleep.' Katya anchors the line on 'understood', while 'got enough sleep' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "О любых проблемах сразу сообщать мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Report any problems to me immediately.' The grammar packs 'about' and 'to me' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "А вот и владелица нашего отеля.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And here is the owner of our hotel.' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'of the hotel' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "eleonora",
      "t": "Я сюда не знакомиться пришла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not come here to get acquainted.' Eleonora brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'here' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
